' A real, ordinary ArcoBASIC program meant to be compiled BY the Fission
' Compiler Substrate's native x86-64 backend (fission/amir/lower_x86_64.abas)
' -- see fission/tests/native_programs/hello_native.abas's own header
' comment for the directory convention. Exercises real TYPED (String)
' arrays -- construction, indexed read/write, ForEach, LEN, PRINT of a
' bare string array (rendering without quotes, matching the oracle
' exactly), and a string array crossing a function boundary (both as a
' parameter, consumed via ForEach, and concatenated across elements). See
' fission/amir/lower_x86_64.abas's own Fission_X86_64IsArrayKind comment
' for the "Array:ElementKind" design.
'
' Expected output verified against legacy `ArcoFission compile-run` on this
' identical source as the equivalence-testing oracle.
FUNCTION Join(arr)
    result = ""
    FOR item IN arr
        result = result + item
    NEXT
    RETURN result
END FUNCTION

names = ["Alice", "Bob", "Carol"]
FOR item IN names
    PRINT item
NEXT
PRINT names[1]
names[1] = "Bobby"
PRINT names[1]
PRINT LEN(names)
PRINT names
PRINT Join(names)
